# {{ .Project.Name }}

{{ .Project.Description }}

This is Aruo's comprehensive, domain-neutral application profile. It provides a modular-monolith server boundary, validated configuration, PostgreSQL migrations, stable public errors, structured request logs, health probes, security headers, a bounded single-process rate limiter, tests, CI, and a production container. It deliberately contains no business entities.

It does not certify the application as production-ready. Read `aruo.yaml` for the exact `SOLVED`, `REQUIRED`, `OPTIONAL`, `DEFERRED`, and `UNKNOWN` record, and read `AGENTS.md` before asking an AI agent to change the repository.

## Start locally

```sh
cp .env.example .env
npm install
docker compose up -d db
npm run db:migrate
npm run dev
```

## Verify

```sh
npm run check
npm run check:security
```

The local gate formats, lints, type-checks, tests, and production-builds the real application. The security audit is separate because it depends on the npm advisory service; CI runs both.

## Before production

Select and test authentication, implement server-side authorization for product data, configure a deployment platform, add a content-security policy matched to actual assets, use a distributed limiter when topology or risk requires it, provide secrets through the platform, and establish backup and restore drills. Add email, jobs, cache, files, analytics, and telemetry only when the product needs them.

Report vulnerabilities privately using `SECURITY.md`. Licensed under {{ .Project.License }}.
